  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Also known as the \"Long Wall of Thrace,\" this fortification line (nearly 60km in length) spanned the Thracian peninsula west of Constantinople. It was built in the 5th century CE and refurbished and modified by the emperor Anastasius in the early 6th century.",
